IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc27-length.l4 -- ccc27 (Criminal Code, Canada, ss 737 to 751.1): the one comparison of a `Length of time` with a number of
-- years that several of the sections below need ("less than two years", "two years or more", "ten years or more").
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The label `s 742.1` is the first section of this range that needs the comparison ("a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years").

§ `Section 742.1 -- a length of time against a number of years`

-- A `Length of time` is years, months, days and a flag for "less a day" (core). Years and months are calendar units, so they
-- are compared as whole months. Days are compared only where they cannot carry into a whole month: the text does not say how
-- many days make a month, so a case where they could is NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: undefined term).
-- src:15864 | 742.1 If a person is convicted of an offence and the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years, the court may, for the purpose of supervising the offender’s behaviour in the community, order that the offender serve the sentence in the community, subject to the conditions imposed under section 742.3, if
@ref s 742.1 "a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years" (src:15864)
GIVEN length IS A `Length of time`, years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1 the length of time is at least that many years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `whole months` GREATER THAN target THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `whole months` EQUALS target AND (length's days GREATER THAN 0 OR NOT (length's `less a day`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `whole months` EQUALS target THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (arithmetic on a length of time against the figure the text names; "two years less a day" is below "two years")
        IF `whole months` PLUS FLOOR (length's days DIVIDED BY 28) AT LEAST target THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): how many days make a month is not stated
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (arithmetic on a length of time against the figure the text names)
    WHERE
        `whole months` MEANS length's years TIMES 12 PLUS length's months
        target MEANS years TIMES 12

-- src:15864 | 742.1 If a person is convicted of an offence and the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years, the court may, for the purpose of supervising the offender’s behaviour in the community, order that the offender serve the sentence in the community, subject to the conditions imposed under section 742.3, if
@ref s 742.1 "a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years" (src:15864)
GIVEN sentence IS AN Imprisonment, years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1 the sentence of imprisonment is at least that many years` MEANS
    CONSIDER sentence
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no term is stated
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN `s 742.1 the length of time is at least that many years` term years
